Changes:
* May 2021: Douglas James leaves Labour to sit as an independent<ref>{{cite web |title=Councillor Douglas James |url=https://cmispublic.walsall.gov.uk/cmis/Councillors/tabid/63/ctl/ViewCMIS_Person/mid/383/id/68/ScreenMode/Party/Default.aspx |website=Walsall.com |access-date=9 April 2022}}</ref>
* July 2021: Harbans Sarohi (Labour) dies; by-election held in December, but winner unable to take seat<ref>{{cite news |last1=Thandi |first1=Gurdip |title='True gentleman' of Walsall politics – due to become mayor next year – dies suddenly |url=https://www.expressandstar.com/news/local-hubs/walsall/2021/07/26/tributes-to-true-gentleman-of-walsall-politics/ |access-date=9 April 2022 |work=expressandstar.com}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Thandi |first1=Gurdip |title=Candidate who couldn't win by-election WINS it and it's pointless |url=https://www.birminghammail.co.uk/black-country/candidate-who-couldnt-win-walsall-22491277 |access-date=9 April 2022 |work=BirminghamLive |date=17 December 2021}}</ref>
* December 2021: Sean Coughlan (Labour) resigns; seat left vacant until 2022 elections<ref>{{cite news |last1=Thandi |first1=Gurdip |title=Ex-council boss quits after child sex offence charges |url=https://www.birminghammail.co.uk/black-country/ex-walsall-council-boss-resigns-22379003 |access-date=9 April 2022 |work=BirminghamLive |date=6 December 2021}}</ref>

